[center][size=6][b]FIND[/b][/size]
[size=4][color=#e8c882]B A S E   S T O R A G E   S E A R C H[/color][/size]

[size=3]Where did I put the Shroud Liquid? Press Shift+F and the chest lights up.[/size][/center]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609966-1205231011.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What it does[/b][/size]

Stand in your base and press [b]Shift+F[/b]. A search box opens, drawn with the game's own dialog, so it looks like part of Enshrouded. Type what you are looking for:
[list]
[*][b]Suggestions as you type[/b], each with how many you have and in how many chests: [i]Granite Block — 996 in 1 chest[/i].
[*][b]Pick with Tab, the arrow keys or the mouse.[/b] The mouse wheel scrolls long lists. [b]Enter[/b] finds.
[*][b]The matching chests pulse[/b] with the game's own highlight, so you can walk straight to them.
[*][b]Open one and the items you searched for glow gold[/b] for a few seconds, every matching slot, so you see them at once in a full chest.
[/list]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609967-2012517538.png[/img]

[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609972-219583874.png[/img][/center]

[line]

[size=4][b]What you can search for[/b][/size]

[center][img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/5811/images/200/200-1792609387-300384686.png[/img][/center]

[list]
[*][b]Items[/b], by the name the game shows. Partial words work: [i]stone[/i] finds Stone and Rough Stone Block.
[*][b]Kinds of items[/b]: categories ([i]Consumables[/i], [i]Ammunition[/i]...), rarities ([i]Uncommon[/i] to [i]Legendary[/i]), item types ([i]One-Handed Axe[/i]...) and perks ([i]Backstab Damage[/i]...). They are labelled in the list, like [i]Perk: Backstab Damage — 12 items in 3 chests[/i].
[*][b]Chest names you gave yourself[/b] with Rename. (The game's own "Storage Chest" titles are not searched, as every unnamed chest would match.)
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Installation[/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Close Enshrouded.
[*]Copy [b]wsock32.dll[/b] into the game folder, next to [i]enshrouded.exe[/i]
(Steam: right-click Enshrouded > Manage > Browse local files).
[*]Start the game, stand inside one of your bases and press [b]Shift+F[/b].
[/list]

[b]Hotkey:[/b] change it in [i]find.ini[/i] in the game folder (written on the first start), for example [i]hotkey = Ctrl+F[/i].

[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete [i]wsock32.dll[/i], plus [i]find.ini[/i] and [i]find.log[/i] if present.

[line]

[size=4][b]Your language[/b][/size]

Find follows the language set in the game. Item, perk, category and rarity names are the game's own. Find's few texts of its own come in English, German, French, Spanish, Italian, Portuguese, Polish, Russian, Ukrainian, Japanese, Korean, Chinese and Turkish. (Corrections from native speakers are welcome.)

[line]

[size=4][b]Compatibility[/b][/size]

[list]
[*][b]Client-side only.[/b] Servers need nothing installed, and other players do not need the mod.
[*][b]Only reads your chests.[/b] It never moves, adds or removes an item.
[*][b]Plays well with other mods.[/b] It uses its own file name, [i]wsock32.dll[/i], and forwards every network call to the real Windows wsock32.dll.
[*][b]Safe on game updates.[/b] Made for the current game version. After an update the mod checks that it still recognises the game; if it does not, it switches itself off (and says so in [i]find.log[/i]) instead of risking a crash.
[*]Opens only while you play or have your backpack open, never while you type in chat, rename something or write on a signpost.
[*]Works with Steam. Not tested with other store versions.
[/list]

[line]

[size=4][b]Known limits[/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Searches the chests of the base you stand in, not all your bases at once.
[/list]

[line]

[size=2]Open source (MIT): [url=https://github.com/Greeneye0/find-enshrouded]github.com/Greeneye0/find-enshrouded[/url]
Made with the help of AI (Claude by Anthropic).[/size]
